{
  "fixture": "bad/reply_cause_invalid.json",
  "contract": "mcp/DISCOVERY_V1.md",
  "kind": "reply",
  "exercises": "The record of good/unavailable_pause_reason.json on a running lease. A reply is the bridge's result for the worker's own final frame, marked reply: true, carrying error_code, error_cause and error_log; the scheduler checks it before it pauses the job (C1). DISCOVERY_UNAVAILABLE needs a cause from the worker's six (segment_corrupt is the store's alone) and RESOURCE_LIMIT one from its ten; any other code carries none. error_log is a discovery log where the cause is about one log, may be left out where the cause takes one optionally, and is absent everywhere else. Each mutant is a protocol failure: the job pauses with READER_PROTOCOL, naming the bad value verbatim, cut to 64 bytes at a character boundary, and nothing is released or stored as a cause; for each of the two codes there is a missing, an unknown and a cross-code cause. After a release, U2 keeps the copied reason and the bad value is logged. The controls pause as before: valid replies, two errors a Node sink threw (packing's RESOURCE_LIMIT and the record bound's 413, each without a cause), a sink's DISCOVERY_UNAVAILABLE that carries its cause and log through to the pause and logs no bad value, and a bridge failure with no worker reply.",
